Three of these five predate OFBIZ-13262 (the May 2026 inventory-reservation feature); two are inside code that feature added.

h3. 1. {{createProductionRunPartyAssign()}} returns the wrong ID
{code:java}
return [successMessage: null, productionRunId: parameters.workEffortId]
{code}
Mini-lang always returned the caller's original {{parameters.productionRunId}}. The Groovy version returns {{parameters.workEffortId}} (post-defaulting), so when a caller assigns a party to a specific *task* (a distinct {{workEffortId}} under the production run), the returned {{productionRunId}} is silently overwritten with the task's ID instead of the real production run's.

h3. 2. {{issueProductionRunTaskComponent()}} NPEs on a missing WorkEffort
{code:java}
GenericValue workEffort = from('WorkEffort').where(workEffortId: parameters.workEffortId).queryOne()
GenericValue productionRun = from('WorkEffort').where(workEffortId: workEffort.workEffortParentId).queryOne()
{code}
No null-check on either lookup; mini-lang's equivalent entity/if-compare tags degrade gracefully on a missing row.

