h3. 1. {{calculateProductCosts()}} throws on a common routing shape
{code:java}
totalCostsByType."${entry.key}" = entry.value + totalCostByType."${entry.key}"
{code}
Typo: {{totalCostByType}} (missing "s") is never declared — the real map is {{totalCostsByType}}. Throws {{MissingPropertyException}} whenever a product's routing has 2+ tasks contributing to the same cost-component type.

h3. 2. {{calculateProductAverageCost()}} lost mini-lang's per-iteration rounding
Mini-lang's {{<calculate>}} elements default to {{decimal-scale="2"}}/{{HALF_EVEN}} when omitted (confirmed in {{Calculate.java}}), so each loop iteration rounds the running total. The Groovy conversion accumulates unrounded and rounds only once at the end. Empirically confirmed with 3 items each contributing 0.125: mini-lang-style yields {{0.36}}, Groovy's single-round yields {{0.38}} — a materially different average cost whenever several inventory items have sub-cent-level contributions.

h3. 3. {{updateProductAverageCostOnReceiveInventory()}} ignores the configured rounding precision
{code:java}
int roundingDecimal = UtilProperties.getPropertyAsInteger('arithmetic', 'finaccout.decimals', 2)
{code}
Typo'd property key ({{finaccout.decimals}}, missing "n") never matches the real {{finaccount.decimals}} key in {{arithmetic.properties}}, so this always silently falls back to the hardcoded default of 2, regardless of what an admin configures.

{{GenericDAO.deleteByCondition()}} builds the WHERE clause of DELETE statements by calling {{condition.makeWhereString(modelEntity, null, this.datasource, sqlP.getDelegator())}}, passing {{null}} as the entity condition params list. {{EntityConditionUtils.addValue()}} treats a null params list as a reason to also drop the {{ModelField}} it was given, even though one is available:

{code:java}
static void addValue(StringBuilder buffer, ModelField field, Object value, List<EntityConditionParam> params) {
    SqlJdbcUtil.addValue(buffer, params == null ? null : field, value, params);
}
{code}

With a null field, {{SqlJdbcUtil.addValueSingle()}} inlines the value into the SQL text as a quoted literal instead of a {{?}} bind parameter, escaping only single quotes ({{value.replace("'", "''")}}), with no backslash handling. On MySQL/MariaDB, whose default {{sql_mode}} treats a backslash inside a string literal as an escape character, a value containing a leading {{\\}} before a quote causes the backslash to consume the closing quote OFBiz just appended, so the rest of the value is parsed as SQL rather than as data. The quote-doubling in place does not account for this.

This path is reachable from every {{Delegator.removeByAnd(...)}} / {{Delegator.removeByCondition(...)}} call (via {{GenericHelperDAO.removeByCondition()}} → {{GenericDAO.deleteByCondition()}}), several of which pass request-derived values in, e.g. {{ProductEvents.removeProductFeatureAppl()}}, reachable via

h3. 1. {{inlineHandlePriceWithTaxIncluded()}} treats an explicit 0% tax rate as "not supplied"
{code:java}
if (!parameters.taxPercentage) {
    ...lookup...
}
if (!parameters.taxPercentage) {
    return error(...'ProductPriceTaxPercentageNotFound')
}
{code}
Mini-lang used {{<if-empty field="parameters.taxPercentage">}}, and {{ObjectType.isEmpty()}} explicitly treats any {{Number}} (including {{BigDecimal}} zero) as non-empty. Groovy's {{!x}} truthiness check treats zero as falsy. A caller explicitly passing {{taxPercentage=0}} (a legitimate tax-exempt rate) now has it silently discarded and re-looked-up, and can fail with "tax percentage not found" for a call that used to succeed.

h3. 2. {{getAssociatedPriceRulesConds()}}'s {{PRIP_CURRENCY_UOMID}} case lost its entity filter
{code:java}
from('Uom').limit(sizeLimit).queryList()
{code}
Mini-lang filtered {{uomTypeId="CURRENCY_MEASURE"}}. The Groovy conversion (via a later refactor, commit a6cfaf87320d) dropped the filter entirely, so the currency dropdown now returns up to 200 arbitrary UOM rows of any type (weight, length, time, etc.) instead of currencies only.

Found via the minilang-to-Groovy regression audit (OFBIZ-13523). One further regression on top of the prior fix (OFBIZ-13577).

h3. {{issueImmediatelyFulfilledOrderItem()}} throws on a nonexistent order/item combination
{code:java}
GenericValue orderItem = parameters.orderItem ?: from('OrderItem').where(parameters).queryOne()
...
if (orderItem.productId) {
