Found two further regressions on top of the prior fixes (OFBIZ-13570, OFBIZ-13583).

h3. 1. {{convertUom()}} skips decimal-scale rounding for a zero-valued conversion
{code:java}
if (convertedValue && roundingMode) {
    convertedValue = convertedValue.setScale(decimalScale as int, roundingMode)
}
{code}
The original mini-lang gated this only on {{roundingMode}}. Groovy's {{convertedValue &&}} is falsy for a zero {{BigDecimal}}, so a legitimate zero-valued conversion returns at the wrong scale (e.g. {{"0E-15"}} instead of {{"0.00"}}).

h3. 2. {{getFileUploadProgressStatus()}} returns a non-integer percentage
{code:java}
result.readPercent = (result.bytesRead * 100) / result.contentLength
{code}
Mini-lang used explicit {{int}} arithmetic; Groovy's {{/}} on two longs returns a full-precision {{BigDecimal}} (e.g. {{77.7777777778}}). Servicedef declares {{readPercent}} as {{Integer}}.

Found via the minilang-to-Groovy regression audit (OFBIZ-13523). 9 regressions in {{ProjectServicesScript.groovy}} vs. the original {{ProjectServices.xml}} mini-lang (OFBIZ-13078):

h3. 1. {{addValidationPartiesToTask()}} always throws
{code:java}
if (from('addValidationPartiesToTask').where(condition).queryCount() == 0) {
{code}
Uses the service's own name as an entity name instead of {{WorkEffortPartyAssignment}}; also drops {{filterByDate()}}. Fires every time a task assignment is completed — always throws.

h3. 2. {{addProjectTimeToInvoice()}} never reuses the existing invoice
{code:java}
boolean createInvoice = !parameters.reCreate
if (parameters.reCreate == 'Y') { ... createInvoice = true //do not create, only add }
{code}
Polarity inverted from the {{reCreate}}/comment intent. {{addProjectTimeToNewInvoice}} (defaults {{reCreate="Y"}}) always mints a new invoice instead of reusing the existing one; {{addProjectTimeToInvoice}} (no {{reCreate}} attribute) is unconditionally {{true}} too, so it never adds to the caller's existing invoice as intended.

